  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to NCI-H2087, suggesting a complex but interconnected pathway. The evidence indicates that Mollicellin N acts on Leukocyte common antigen, which is a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, and this compound further targets NCI-H2087. Similarly, Mollicellin N also targets A704, which is a target of the same compound, reinforcing the link between Mollicellin N and NCI-H2087. Additionally, Mollicellin N interacts with P2X purinoceptor 1, which is targeted by a different compound that also leads to NCI-H2087. These findings suggest that Mollicellin N may exert its effects through multiple distinct mechanisms, all of which ultimately contribute to the interaction with NCI-H2087. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Mollicellin N to influence NCI-H2087 through various molecular targets, underscoring the importance of understanding the diverse roles of this compound in biological processes.",
